This skill is DISTRIBUTED, not resident.

`scripts/persist-skill.ts` degit-copies `cloudflare/skills/skills/turnstile-spin` into other
people's repositories, where this repo's package.json / bun.lock / node_modules do not exist.
Any bare import here would resolve during development and THROW for the user who persisted it
— measured 2026-07-28: an inline or bare specifier fails on the SCRIPT's location, not on cwd.

So everything under this directory stays zero-dep: node:/bun: builtins only, `parseArgs` for
flags, no `type-flag`, no graduation dependency of any kind. `scripts/script-check.ts` enforces
it by finding this marker (writing-bun-scripts BG3).

Second reason, independent of the first: this skill is a mirror of Cloudflare's upstream skill.
Diverging its scripts from upstream costs more than the typing buys.
